OracleRecovery
├── A guard can directly apply the latest authenticated rejected report
│   ├── Recovery updates NAV and settles withdrawals without another forwarder delivery
│   ├── Unseen future reports and already-consumed reports cannot be approved
│   ├── Malformed bytes and changes to any cached report field cannot authorize recovery
│   ├── A newer valid report replaces the cached candidate while the oracle remains frozen
│   └── Invalid destinations, nonces and snapshots cannot replace the cached candidate
├── Clearing recovery state does not change accounting
│   ├── Empty unfreeze clears the cache and retains the previous NAV, cutoff and batches
│   ├── Normal acceptance after empty unfreeze keeps the rejection cache empty
│   └── Manual freeze and workflow cutover invalidate the cached candidate
└── Direct recovery retains all non-movement checks
    ├── Delivery age is checked again, including its exact maximum boundary
    ├── Curator age is checked again and failed recovery preserves the candidate
    └── Withdrawals require live funding and settle at most once after funding arrives
